## Frontend implementation contract

### Source ownership

Name the frontend source roots, maintainers, review route, generated-source boundaries, and ownership handoff. Cite the repository paths or decisions that establish each confirmed statement.

### Framework, routing, and components

Record the confirmed framework and version, entry points, routing and navigation model, component boundaries, composition rules, and any browser or platform support constraints. Keep candidates and unverified versions Proposed or Open.

### State and data fetching

Record client state, server or cache state, data-fetching boundaries, loading and cancellation semantics, freshness or invalidation rules, and the owner of each interface. Link the source contract or design decision; do not infer behavior from a filename or dependency alone.

### Forms and styling

Record form ownership, validation and submission behavior, error presentation, styling or theming approach, responsive constraints, and any design-system relationship. Route visual and interaction principles back to `DESIGN.md`.

### Accessibility and performance

Record confirmed keyboard, focus, semantics, assistive-technology, reduced-motion, localization, browser-support, performance-budget, and measurement expectations. Name the project-owned checks or review evidence that establish them.

### Client-side loading, errors, and retries

Describe the user-visible loading, empty, error, timeout, offline, cancellation, and retry states. State retry limits, idempotency assumptions, recovery affordances, and escalation to the owning interface only when those facts are confirmed. Do not use this section to claim service availability or operational recovery.

## Project-owned verification boundary

`QUALITY.md` is the current authority for project-owned checks. For frontend changes, record the exact applicable lint, type, unit, integration, browser, accessibility, visual, and performance checks, their candidate identity, result, and supporting artifact in the active Plan. A fresh Verification Sub checks the integrated candidate read-only and reports criterion-level evidence; this document does not execute checks or establish a passing result merely by naming one.

## Constraints and non-goals

- Do not infer framework, routes, components, state behavior, form rules, accessibility support, or performance results from scanner output, provenance, filenames, or dependencies.
- Keep service and deployed-runtime reliability in the subordinate `RELIABILITY.md`/`OPERATIONS.md` route rather than expanding this document into an operations authority.
- Keep product intent in `PRODUCT.md`, universal visual and interaction principles in `DESIGN.md`, and implementation work state in a project-owned Plan.
- Do not place credentials, tokens, private data, or unsupported claims here.
- This document is descriptive project guidance; it is not an executor, permission grant, health guarantee, or substitute for project-owned verification.
